Z||000053||DaRkLoRD||02-05-2001||02:03 AM||||<I>Warning: useless info ahead</I><P>I remember hearing about the Challenger in school, I was in grade 1.. don't recall anything specific about that day though.<BR>I was in my kitchen with my sister when the fighting broke out in the gulf war.. I remember vanilla ice, MC Hammer.. rat tails (used to have that hair style.. hey, don't laugh.. I was 9...) I have a Colecovision somewhere still, and an original Nintendo.. I remember those cool canvas shoes.. I even remember when Reebok introduced "Black Top" running shoes.. I still have the plastic tag, I use it as a keychain.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (that was back when I still wore running shoes, now I wear boots.) also..<BR>-ninja turtles<BR>-fat albert (hey hey hey!!)<BR>-ghostbusters, the cartoon<BR>-peewee's playhouse<P>If the Apollo program in 1969 had the equivilant of a 486, why do the space shuttles now only have 386s?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000054||FieroMaster88||02-05-2001||02:55 AM||||Damn, I am 19, and I know quite a few of them.......I have a black and white TV with like 22 channels, does that count?  I still have an Atari 2600, pong is great, packman rocks!  I like pitfall the best though.  I own a record player, and I have some Michael Jackson records from when he was black, Got some of his 8 tracks and a player too (suprise, suprise)!  Have you ever watched Nick at Night???  I dont have an answering machine now, we had a typerwriter, i could use it, McDonalds still surves some breakfast food in styrofoam containers and yes, I know who Kansas, Chicago, Boston and alabama are because remember, we do have parents!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I think the Michael Jackson one was the best.......... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||1
Z||000055||FieroMaster88||02-05-2001||03:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>I remember my old 386 computer.  My first games were Police Quest and Doom.  Police quest was awesome, it had a 1-900 number to call for hints, my parents were pissed when they saw the phone bill! (2.99 a min.)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>386?????  My first computer was a 286 I got from my dad when he got his 486 about 2 years ago.  We upgraded my 286 to a 386, then I got the 486.  Well, now I have a Pentium 166 but i am buying a pentium 800, man, how quickly things change.   OOH, by the way, i still have poliece quest and Doom on my computer.  Those are the best. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||1
